    "3. How Your Data Is Stored: Guest or Account",
    "• Guest: Your plan, progress and settings are stored only on your phone. Nothing is uploaded. Deleting the app, clearing its data, or using Profile > Erase data on this phone erases them.\n• Account: Your data is saved in one private record that belongs to your account (Google Cloud Firestore), protected by security rules so that only you, signed in, can read or change it. Changes sync a few seconds after you make them.\n• Creating an account keeps what you already did as a guest. Signing in to an existing account shows that account's own data on the phone instead.\n• Signing out removes your data from the phone. It stays in your account, ready for your next sign-in.",
